#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161745 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "6d3ad56f-a242-5335-aa48-e2608b1b973d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16584" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(1\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/f3/f3440005b2b4e7ce1cc2eed5825d11cb309522a6807bcd18ffada189fadd0cda.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/1f/1f2f28b0f36aeb85a07076e1507c9561b707bf7d00de727998b02075b5458da4.svg)\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.8647\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161746 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "f1adfc5c-78aa-5f14-bec5-cf763d86e5af" :question/math-academy-id "e-16585" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(\\dfrac 23\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/49/49fa146efc8029727469bc5909c2a946c9cb96383976d4096d455b423a428479.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( \\dfrac 23 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/72/721ca1810b816431f99bb8294f4ad12ff125342640a925035487c8ecace4eff6.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x/3}|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161747 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "fffe6dba-c0a1-5644-a975-6d51b6de2f98" :question/math-academy-id "e-16586" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(2\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e7/e77daa45c1026175eec99e71cb336ad5b8c2a46683170b0f9357a4ad7e9d1bf5.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 2 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e0/e0b6d1388350fabce97f26601d512e60cfe6ac3ab41230671718ca034c5c3860.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<2) & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x}|}_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4}+{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.3496\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161748 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/id #uuid "88232e58-999e-5ac8-8f09-8a4b204ec51c" :question/math-academy-id "e-16587" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(4\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\leq 7 \\, \\bigg |\\, X > 5\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda)$ and two positive real numbers $s, t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = P(X > t) = e^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\leq s+t \\, \\big|\\, X>s) = 1-P(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = 1-e^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda = 4,$ $s=5,$ and $s+t=7.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt = (t+s) - s =7 - 5 = 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7\\,|\\,X>5) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(4)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-8} \\\\  & ≈0.999\\,664.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15122c8a-6495-57b5-bc9a-8504dc7b9d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3927" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424528} {:answer/id #uuid "a2cad5b5-d85b-5775-9ae3-23738e9a9e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3279" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424550} {:answer/id #uuid "adb828a8-83fa-5e72-8b2f-372fd52cbd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3337" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424551} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb85eac-0073-5d12-9fad-bb5b6c84c2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3297" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424552} {:answer/id #uuid "b07b0fbc-b758-5397-9f9a-f0c56f381e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3137" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb85eac-0073-5d12-9fad-bb5b6c84c2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3297" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424552} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f87a4b8-066c-5da9-b676-ea815d24ff9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "377d9ecb-b1f2-5b7d-b293-34044d6f6558" :question/math-academy-id "q-132173" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x/5}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2/5}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.3297\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc40c2d-1af0-5adc-a2bc-6557e8adc194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4683" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424533} {:answer/id #uuid "31011ded-b236-51be-8752-9a8a39f1aa2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4836" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424534} {:answer/id #uuid "3a08e9d4-be37-5bcd-b93a-f75705061f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4886" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424535} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6f8763-9d72-5754-bbed-ce927bc4b0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4768" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424537} {:answer/id #uuid "47bc7314-1895-551e-8d2a-b165d99e961e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4386" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47bc7314-1895-551e-8d2a-b165d99e961e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4386" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424540} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc8a138-558e-5ca1-bd83-4c4ce4806474" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b3ef3ac-d2db-5eb8-8c5f-a033b26be69b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132179" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.4386\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25462498-9604-5abf-a03e-8496f16cbe50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424530} {:answer/id #uuid "68d43eaf-e9d2-5c03-90f1-2c5494830081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1435" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424544} {:answer/id #uuid "a0dfb2f8-0b7f-57b3-99b5-9e1f339559e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1553" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424548} {:answer/id #uuid "b69c52c0-8e2e-5c56-a7ce-24a1cf21399a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1155" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424554} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1596e7-46b5-53ff-8622-206707f0ad5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1233" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25462498-9604-5abf-a03e-8496f16cbe50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424530} :answer-field/id #uuid "30cd8153-4b27-59dd-bd60-d805ce68023b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04d4be2b-e767-5839-99c5-470d8cac4dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132193" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}),$ calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\sqrt{2}) & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016959b9-f05f-53b3-afd3-07e994e53882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424525} {:answer/id #uuid "17f972c0-e3f4-509a-b28c-755fd028d943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424529} {:answer/id #uuid "8012b58b-be32-5887-bb98-32352b39ab18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424546} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424555} {:answer/id #uuid "c54104af-76de-56d8-9541-8d02ef24fb4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424555} :answer-field/id #uuid "13285fe0-63a3-5aa6-b3a7-7b2fe9fce9be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15d3a8f7-57e9-5955-b347-e7b15292f88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253935" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(3),$ calculate $P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3,$ $s=\\frac{2}{3},$ and $s+t=\\frac{5}{6}.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=\\frac{5}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3)\\cdot (1/6)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25fb97a5-9ed6-5c98-8031-485552414117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-5{e}^{-3/5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424531} {:answer/id #uuid "4cbd30f8-0317-54c7-8a80-7f23503ecca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424542} {:answer/id #uuid "5151c7de-e2f6-5856-b422-07c5dab2d5f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424543} {:answer/id #uuid "e5bcecd5-8331-5e54-9822-a05d7243d9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-1/5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424560} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b3ce16-7f1a-5313-be26-0788d6b661a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5151c7de-e2f6-5856-b422-07c5dab2d5f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424543} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0a548f-8bd4-50d5-8207-5dc86f15188f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a86905dc-6d69-50e5-afb3-4d8bb353dbfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-253936" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{5},$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-4=5\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3/5)\\cdot (5)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a2b804-976b-516e-8262-d27bd168e200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1155" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424539} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f19cf2-ae03-5a5d-a484-a5c96a8a6ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1328" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424549} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c9e78d-99e5-5ab7-9783-9080b7da6c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1951" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424556} {:answer/id #uuid "e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1455" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424561} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ab51fe-7288-559d-9763-4a92ffa3e0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1785" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1455" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424561} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" :question/math-academy-id "q-96347" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ calculate $P(2<X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X<3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.1455\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424526} {:answer/id #uuid "2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9592" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424532} {:answer/id #uuid "404222de-38b1-5509-b195-dc8a8808dc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0489" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424538} {:answer/id #uuid "70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0408" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424545} {:answer/id #uuid "c786b93e-93f4-53da-8bd9-45ac133e7e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0408" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424545} :answer-field/id #uuid "693fb341-39fe-5150-9137-34fee2604c10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be9c7f67-1bb2-5f32-8555-0a5418fba86d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96412" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(8),$ calculate $P(X>0.4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(8).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>0.4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0.4) & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-8x}{|}_{0.4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈0.0408\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4411" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424527} {:answer/id #uuid "3b282901-4897-5136-9d46-9253c88fc7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424536} {:answer/id #uuid "486ea7b8-8768-5c1b-9819-16e84f6ed54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4852" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424541} {:answer/id #uuid "8451cd55-2a53-5891-9ae6-f129b4cd4ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4799" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424547} {:answer/id #uuid "ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4712" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4712" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424559} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96421" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.5\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-0.5} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
